 "title": "Centre of Gravity",
 "author": "Claude (experimental setter)",
 "rules": "Normal sudoku rules apply. SEESAWS (invented): each brown line is a seesaw resting on the circled cell, its fulcrum. Every other digit on the line pushes its side down with a force equal to the digit times its distance from the fulcrum, counted in cells along the line (the cells next to the fulcrum count x1, the next ones x2, and so on). Each seesaw balances: the total on one side of the fulcrum equals the total on the other side. The digit in the fulcrum itself does not count. Example: 9 | fulcrum | 1 4 balances, since 9x1 = 1x1 + 4x2.",
